#!/bin/sh
# Pick a command from ~/.config/herdr/launchers.tsv with fzf and run it in a
# new Herdr workspace; text that matches no entry starts claude with the
# text as its first prompt. The workspace closes when the command exits.
#
# Each line of the file is "label<TAB>command"; lines starting with # are
# ignored.

set -eu

herdr=${HERDR_BIN_PATH:-herdr}
launchers=${HERDR_LAUNCHERS:-$HOME/.config/herdr/launchers.tsv}
cwd=${HERDR_ACTIVE_PANE_CWD:-$HOME}

# --print-query prints the typed text first, then the selection if any.
# fzf exits 1 when nothing matched, in which case the text is the prompt.
status=0
out=$(grep -v '^#' "$launchers" | cut -f1 |
    fzf --no-sort --reverse --prompt='launch> ' --print-query) || status=$?
query=$(printf '%s\n' "$out" | sed -n 1p)
label=$(printf '%s\n' "$out" | sed -n 2p)

if [ "$status" = 0 ]; then
    command=$(awk -F'\t' -v label="$label" '$1 == label { print $2; exit }' "$launchers")
elif [ "$status" = 1 ] && [ -n "$query" ]; then
    quoted=$(printf '%s' "$query" | sed "s/'/'\\\\''/g")
    command="claude '$quoted'"
else
    exit 0
fi

pane=$("$herdr" workspace create --cwd "$cwd" --focus |
    jq -r .result.root_pane.pane_id)
# An entry without a command leaves the workspace's own shell.
if [ -n "$command" ]; then
    "$herdr" pane run "$pane" "exec $command" >/dev/null
fi
